1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,050
You're looking at Custer's last cry for

2
00:00:02,050 --> 00:00:05,080
help. 210 lives depended on it.

3
00:00:05,370 --> 00:00:06,760
So why did help never come?

4
00:00:07,234 --> 00:00:11,174
June 25, 1876. Custer reached the hills

5
00:00:11,174 --> 00:00:13,274
above the Little Bighorn and finally saw

6
00:00:13,274 --> 00:00:14,784
the village. It was enormous.

7
00:00:15,474 --> 00:00:17,524
He had already split his regiment in three.

8
00:00:17,974 --> 00:00:19,924
Now he needed every man he had.

9
00:00:20,316 --> 00:00:21,696
His trumpeter, John Martin,

10
00:00:21,696 --> 00:00:24,256
was an Italian immigrant who barely spoke

11
00:00:24,256 --> 00:00:26,716
English. So the adjutant wrote the order

12
00:00:26,716 --> 00:00:27,186
down.

13
00:00:27,570 --> 00:00:29,410
Martin galloped back along the trail,

14
00:00:29,410 --> 00:00:31,520
as fast as his horse could run.

15
00:00:31,908 --> 00:00:33,578
“Benteen. Come on. Big village.

16
00:00:33,648 --> 00:00:34,578
Be quick. Bring packs.”

17
00:00:35,362 --> 00:00:36,372
Packs meant the mules.

18
00:00:36,682 --> 00:00:38,072
They carried the reserve ammunition.

19
00:00:38,813 --> 00:00:40,483
Captain Benteen got the note.

20
00:00:40,853 --> 00:00:43,133
He rode on, but found Major Reno's men shattered

21
00:00:43,133 --> 00:00:44,573
on a hill. He stopped.

22
00:00:44,573 --> 00:00:46,403
And waited for the pack train.

23
00:00:46,894 --> 00:00:48,184
More than an hour passed.

24
00:00:48,774 --> 00:00:51,434
Custer and about 210 men were never seen

25
00:00:51,434 --> 00:00:52,204
alive again.

26
00:00:52,664 --> 00:00:54,924
Martin was one of the last soldiers to see

27
00:00:54,924 --> 00:00:57,284
Custer alive. Should Benteen have ridden

28
00:00:57,284 --> 00:00:58,864
on? Read the note again,

29
00:00:58,864 --> 00:00:59,714
and tell me.

